# resource-generation-flows

The resource generation system implements specialized content creation workflows for both professional case management and client-facing materials.

## Resource Generation Core Components

1. Client Resource Generation
Path: app/api/generate-client-resource/route.ts
- Produces specialized therapeutic materials (worksheets, reading materials, exercises)
- Adapts content based on trauma-informed language requirements
- Formats resources according to client context and resource type
Importance Score: 85/100

2. Treatment Plan Generation
Path: app/api/generate-plan/route.ts
- Creates case plans using multi-stage context building
- Integrates knowledge base best practices with local provider data
- Applies client-specific context and urgency prioritization
Importance Score: 90/100 

3. Knowledge Management
Path: app/api/knowledge/route.ts
- Maintains treatment protocols and best practices database
- Formats organizational knowledge for AI prompts
- Manages local partnerships and referral pathways
Importance Score: 75/100

## Resource Types and Formats

1. Professional Resources
- Case plans with intervention strategies
- Treatment provider recommendations
- Evidence-based practice documentation
- Clinical guidelines and protocols

2. Client Resources  
- Therapeutic worksheets
- Reading materials
- Skill-building exercises
- Action planning templates

The system emphasizes trauma-informed content generation and context-aware formatting based on resource type and intended audience.

